.²9 ({#nam, nA#}) (<ab>Rhet.</ab>) A suggested meaning; also the process by which
 such meaning is suggested. It is the power of suggestion (founded on {#aBiDA#}
 or {#lakzaRA#} denotation or indication), by which something else is understood
 from a word which, though having more meanings than one, has been restricted
 to a single meaning by relations of conjunction, disjunction <ab>&c.</ab> ({#saMyoga#},
 {#viprayoga, sAhacarya, viroDitA#} <ab>&c.</ab>), or, briefly, the use of a word
 of several meanings in a special sense determined by the context; {%<ab>e. g.</ab>%}
 {#saSaNGacakro hariH#} the adjective restricts Hari to mean ‘Viṣṇu’
 alone, and not a ‘lion’ or ‘monkey’; so {#rAmalakzmaRO dASaraTI, rAmArjunO#}
 {#BArgavakArtavIryO#} <ab>&c.</ab>; <ab>cf.</ab> {#anekArTasya Sabdasya vAcakatve niyantrite .#}
 {#saMyogAdyEravAcyArTaDIkfd vyApftiraYjanam ..#} <ls>K. P. 2.</ls>; <ls>S. D. 23-6</ls>;
